+Example: run evaluations with thresholds.
+
+```ts
+import { Eval } from 'frai-core';
+
+const dataset = Eval.loadDataset({
+  outputsPath: './outputs.json',
+  referencesPath: './references.json'
+});
+
+const evaluations = Eval.runEvaluations({
+  outputs: dataset.outputs,
+  references: dataset.references
+});
+
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  outputsPath: dataset.outputsPath,
+  referencesPath: dataset.referencesPath,
+  thresholds: {
+    exact_match: 0.9,
+    toxicity: 0.8
+  }
+});
+
+const path = Eval.writeReport({ report, format: 'json' });
+console.log(`Report: ${path}, Passed: ${report.passed}`);
+```
+
 Because `frai-core` is a regular ESM package, you can import only the modules you need and embed FRAI capabilities inside automation pipelines, CI jobs, or custom products.
 
